Subject: [PATCH 1/2] =?UTF-8?q?dos:=20Phase=2010=20patch=200042=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20MPU-401=20probe=20defensive=20bailout=20(real-HW)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

W22-WB-C operator iter (2026-05-06) hit a hard system lockup at WB
backend init: WB.LOG ended at the engine-side line "wb backend
probing port 0x0330 for MPU-401..." with no subsequent SDL-side or
engine-side log. Operator hard-reset twice, same lockup both times.
DOSBox-X had passed the path cleanly because the emulated MPU-401
ACKs reset on the same wire schedule the original probe assumed.

The original SDL/0037 SDL_DOSMpu401Init used an SDL_GetTicksNS()-
based 10ms wall-clock deadline + inb-poll for the 0xFE ACK byte.
Two failure-mode hypotheses for why this hung indefinitely on real
Vibra16S CT2490 + DreamBlaster S2:

  (a) ISA bus stall on the status-port read, or on the reset
      outportb itself. Some chips can pull IOCHRDY low when accessed
      in pathological state, blocking the bus until released.
  (b) Pathological interaction with SDL3's timer source —
      SDL_GetTicksNS internally re-enters or returns stale values
      under some real-HW IRQ contention, deadline never expires.

Both hypotheses point to the same defensive fix: don't rely on the
chip's responsiveness OR on the timer source for the loop bound.

Three changes:

  1. Open-bus early-exit. Read the status register ONCE before
     issuing reset. If it returns 0xFF (canonical ISA open-bus
     pattern when no chip decodes the address), bail with false
     immediately. Avoids issuing reset to a non-responsive chip
     entirely. This handles hypothesis (a) for the case where
     the chip isn't there at all (e.g., daughterboard not
     installed or BLASTER P-field misconfigured).

  2. Replace SDL_GetTicksNS()-deadline with a hard iteration cap.
     20000 iterations × ~500ns per inportb on Pentium ≈ 10ms wall-
     clock — same upper bound as the original deadline, but
     terminates regardless of timer-source state. Eliminates the
     entire class of "timer dies, loop spins forever" failures
     described in hypothesis (b).

  3. doskutsu_dbg_log entry/exit observability. Engine's WB.LOG
     only had "probing port..." with no SDL-side log of probe
     entry/exit/result. Adding three doskutsu_dbg_log lines (entry,
     early-exit-on-0xFF, no-ACK-after-N-iter, ok-after-N-iter)
     means the next real-HW iter has SDL-side log evidence to
     pinpoint exactly which step hangs if the defensive fix
     isn't sufficient.

Validation: DOSBox-X smoke is explicitly insufficient per memory
dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md. This patch needs an operator-
iter cycle on real Vibra16S+S2 to confirm. The previous shipping
binary's lockup will return on real HW unless this fix actually
addresses one of the two hypothesized failure modes.

Companion: SDL/0043 (CloseDevice DSP hard-reset for the related
W22-WB-C #44 force-pause quit lockup) ships in the same iter.
---
 src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c | 68 ++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 54 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
index 2950355fc..e1bb0555a 100644
--- a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
+++ b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
@@ -62,30 +62,70 @@ static int s_mpu401_port_base = -1;
 
 bool SDL_DOSMpu401Init(uint16_t port_base)
 {
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("mpu401: probe entry port_base=0x%04x", (unsigned)port_base);
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0042): open-bus early-exit. Read
+       the status register BEFORE issuing the reset write. If it returns
+       0xFF, that's the canonical "no chip is decoding this address" /
+       open-bus pattern on ISA — bail with false immediately rather than
+       writing reset to a non-responsive port. This avoids the W22-WB-C
+       lockup failure mode where issuing reset to a non-responsive chip
+       stalled the ISA bus indefinitely on real Vibra16S CT2490
+       (the failure was distinct from the inb-poll loop spinning; the
+       outportb write itself appears to have hung). */
+    const Uint8 initial_status = inportb((Uint16)(port_base + 1));
+    if (initial_status == 0xFF) {
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("mpu401: probe early-exit (status=0xFF; no chip at 0x%04x)",
+                         (unsigned)port_base);
+        return false;
+    }
+
     /* Reset MPU-401: write 0xFF to command port (data + 1). */
     outportb((Uint16)(port_base + 1), 0xFF);
 
-    /* Poll for ACK (0xFE) on data port within ~10 ms wall-clock.
-       Status bit 7 (0x80) = data-set-ready (read input available). */
-    const Uint64 deadline = SDL_GetTicksNS() + SDL_MS_TO_NS(10);
-    while (SDL_GetTicksNS() < deadline) {
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0042): poll for ACK (0xFE) with a
+       hard ITERATION CAP rather than an SDL_GetTicksNS()-based wall-
+       clock deadline. The original 10ms deadline approach hung
+       indefinitely on real Vibra16S+S2 hardware in W22-WB-C iter (WB.LOG
+       ended at the engine-side "probing port..." line with no further
+       output, including no SDL-side log). Suspected: either ISA bus
+       stall on the status-port read, or a pathological interaction with
+       SDL3's timer source. The iteration cap is a known-bounded code
+       path that terminates regardless of timer-source state.
+
+       Sizing: 20000 iterations × ~500ns per inportb on Pentium ≈ 10ms
+       wall-clock — same upper bound as the original deadline, but
+       without the timer dependency. Status bit 7 (0x80) = DSR (data-
+       set-ready inverse: low = data available to read). */
+    bool ack_ok = false;
+    int iter;
+    for (iter = 0; iter < 20000; iter++) {
         const Uint8 status = inportb((Uint16)(port_base + 1));
         if ((status & 0x80) == 0) { /* DSR low = byte ready to read */
             const Uint8 ack = inportb(port_base);
             if (ack == 0xFE) {
-                /* Enter UART mode. After this, all writes to data port
-                   pass directly to MIDI bus; status bit 6 (0x40) = DRR
-                   (data ready to receive; must be 0 before each write). */
-                outportb((Uint16)(port_base + 1), 0x3F);
-                /* Some clones don't ACK the UART-mode command per
-                   docs/PHASE10-DESIGN.md § C.2 step 4; we don't require
-                   a second ACK. */
-                s_mpu401_port_base = (int)port_base;
-                return true;
+                ack_ok = true;
+                break;
             }
         }
     }
-    return false;
+
+    if (!ack_ok) {
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("mpu401: probe failed (no 0xFE ACK after %d iter; "
+                         "port=0x%04x)", iter, (unsigned)port_base);
+        return false;
+    }
+
+    /* Enter UART mode. After this, all writes to data port pass
+       directly to MIDI bus; status bit 6 (0x40) = DRR (data ready
+       to receive; must be 0 before each write). Some clones don't
+       ACK the UART-mode command per docs/PHASE10-DESIGN.md § C.2
+       step 4; we don't require a second ACK. */
+    outportb((Uint16)(port_base + 1), 0x3F);
+    s_mpu401_port_base = (int)port_base;
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("mpu401: probe ok (UART mode active at 0x%04x; "
+                     "ack after %d iter)", (unsigned)port_base, iter);
+    return true;
 }
 
 void SDL_DOSMpu401WriteByte(uint8_t byte)
